// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// icons.js - the shell's own vector icons (all drawn on a 100 x 100 grid).
//
// Every icon is a list of SVG path strings, normally just one. A few icons
// are split into several parts so they can be lit partially:
//
//   signal : 4 bars, left (shortest) to right (tallest)
//   volume : [0] speaker, [1] inner wave, [2] outer wave
//   battery: [0] the whole battery shape (the charge is clipped in QML)
//   wifi-arcs: [0] dot, [1] small arc, [2] middle arc, [3] big arc (signal strength);
//              "wifi" is the same icon in one piece (the island button)
//
// "wifi" and "bluetooth" are your Icon_wifi.svg / Icon_bluetooth.svg. The
// "bt-..." icons (headphones, mouse, keyboard, gamepad, phone, speaker, laptop:
// the device types of the Bluetooth list) and "ethernet" (the cable row of the
// Wi-Fi list) are drawn for the shell in the same solid style.
//
// These were converted from the icon files you supplied. "pause" was not in
// the set, so it is drawn here in the same rounded style as "play"; "moon"
// (suspend, used by the lock screen when its theme is missing) likewise.
// "picker" (the colour picker block, top right) is your Icon_Color_picker.svg, in
// absolute coordinates (Qt misreads a relative "m" right after a "z").
// The paths were cleaned of self-overlaps so every renderer fills them the same way.
// The "chev-..." arrows are drawn for the calendar; "search" (the search field),
// "set-island", "set-dock" and "set-wallpaper" (the frame with its notch / its bar / a
// picture of hills and a sun), "set-theme" (a painter's palette, traced from your
// picture), "set-appearance" (a ring, its right half filled), "set-blur" (dots, smaller
// towards the edge) and "set-system" (the gear of the Settings app's own icon,
// assets/icons/frame-settings.svg), "set-devices" (a keyboard), "set-screenshot" (the
// four corners of a selection round a dot), "set-keybinds" (the command key's sign,
// four loops round a square: its holes drawn the other way round): pages of the Settings app.
// "power-logo" (four rounded corners of a frame, your drawing made even: 14 wide, round ends,
// outer corners 17 round, inner ones 3) is the bottom bar's power button; "power" stays the
// sign for shutting down (the power menu, the lock screen)
// (its Notifications page uses "bell-fill"); "mic" (a microphone: the Devices page's input);
// "note-save" (a floppy disk, traced
// from your reference picture) for the quick note's Save button. "bin" (a bin with its lid,
// two slots in it) removes a wallpaper you added (the Settings app). "apps" (four rounded
// squares: the Appearance page's app icons) and "info" (an "i" in a circle: the System page's
// About card) head cards of the Settings app. "set-presets" (a stack of three layers: a
// diamond and two chevrons under it) is the Settings app's Presets page.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

